//   dodges it on its jets, ankles and wing alight: up over a flat shot, aside from one coming down;
//   and its guns, pointing the other way from the jets, fire back down the round's way; then it does
//   not dodge again for a while;
// - a blast throws it a little and hurts it; a hard landing does; what falls on it strikes it; its
//   armour gone, it falls apart burning - its fuel and power cell in flames, no blast beyond its own
